      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's unnerving, I know, but you can't always predict exactly *where* a tiny, mischievous error will hide, much like predicting which patch of moss will grow on a specific rock face. However, these issues often cluster around specific areas, like where you handle third-party integrations or complex data transformations. You can predict risk by focusing your scrutiny on those high-risk zones—think of them as the known, dark corners of your digital cave system.\n\nFor instance, any custom API calls or scripts that interact with external services are prime locations for hidden data leakage. A regular, thorough code review focused specifically on input validation and data retention policies in those integration points is your best bet for proactive defense. These aren't just random errors; they are usually the result of a specific, overlooked interaction.",
